 Priority-Based CPU Scheduling Algorithm:-
BEGIN
    INPUT process_list

    WHILE process_list is NOT EMPTY DO
        SORT process_list BY priority DESCENDING

        SELECT process WITH highest priority

        ALLOCATE CPU TIME to selected process
        EXECUTE process

        IF process is completed THEN
            REMOVE process from process_list
        ELSE
            REDUCE priority slightly
            ADD process back to process_list
        ENDIF
    ENDWHILE

    PRINT "All processes completed"
END

Purpose: Gives CPU time to high-priority processes while gradually lowering the priority of processes that continue running, helping prevent starvation.

