RAM Resource Management Among Virtual Machines:-
BEGIN
    total_RAM = 16GB
    host_reserved = 4GB
    available_RAM = total_RAM - host_reserved

    INPUT number_of_VMs
    min_RAM = 2GB

    FOR i = 1 TO number_of_VMs DO
        IF available_RAM >= min_RAM THEN
            ALLOCATE min_RAM to VM[i]
            available_RAM = available_RAM - min_RAM
        ELSE
            PRINT "Insufficient memory for VM[i]"
        ENDIF
    ENDFOR

    PRINT "Remaining RAM =", available_RAM
END

Purpose: Reserves memory for the host and distributes the remaining RAM fairly among virtual machines while ensuring each VM receives at least 2 GB when possible.

